# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc asinasln, asinhasln, asinh. The ln forms -i*ln(i*x+sqrt(1-x^2)) (asin, and acos = pi/2-asin) and ln(x+sqrt(x^2+1)) (asinh) add two terms of size |x| and opposite sign when |x| is large and x lies on the cancelling side (asin: im(x)>0, or x real and negative; asinh: re(x)<0, or x on the imaginary axis below 0), so acos(-10^20+1/2) gave 3.14159265359-21.4875625974*i (right 3.14159265359-46.7448490404*i) and asinh(-10^1250) a value with no right digit. Both functions are odd, in their ln forms too ((i*x+s)*(-i*x+s) = 1 and neither factor is a negative real), so on that side the value is taken as -f(-x), the same number without the cancellation. The side is read from the double of x, for |x| > 1 (below, the sum is at least sqrt(2)-1 in size); a symbolic x keeps its form.
--- a/src/usual.cc
+++ b/src/usual.cc
@@ -2150,7 +2150,31 @@
